hadiths[115]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3450","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Isa bin Maryam (peace be upon him) saw a man stealing and asked him: 'Did you steal?' He said: 'Not at all, by the One besides whom there is no true god!' So Isa (peace be upon him) said: 'I believe in Allah and I deny my own eye.'"
"3451","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""My mother saw (in a dream) as though a light came out of her, by which the palaces of Syria (al-Sham) were illuminated."
"3452","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The head of disbelief is towards the east. Pride and arrogance are found among the owners of horses and camels, that is, the loud-voiced people of wabar (the nomadic bedouins), and tranquillity is found among the owners of sheep and goats."
"3453","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The head of disbelief is from here, from where the horn of Satan rises (that is, from the east)."
"3454","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Stand close together in the rows, for Satan stands in the gaps (in the rows)."
"3455","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Make your rows close together, bring them near to one another and keep your necks level."
"3456","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The dream of a believer is one part of the forty parts of prophethood. It (the dream) remains like a bird (suspended in the air) as long as it is not related; when it is related, it falls. So do not relate it except to an intelligent person or to someone who loves you (a well-wisher)."
"3457","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The dream of a believer is one part of the forty-six parts of prophethood."
"3458","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The dream of a believer is one part of the forty-six parts of prophethood. It remains like a bird (suspended in the air) as long as it is not related, and when it is related, it comes to pass."
"3459","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The dream of a righteous Muslim is one part of the seventy parts of prophethood."
"3460","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the night I was taken on the Night Journey (Mi'raj), I saw Ibrahim (peace be upon him). He said: 'O Muhammad, convey my greetings of peace to your Ummah and tell them that the soil of Paradise is pure and its water is sweet, that it is a level plain, and that its plants are: Subhan Allah (Glory be to Allah), wal-hamdu lillah (and praise be to Allah), wa la ilaha illa Allah (and there is no god but Allah), wallahu akbar (and Allah is the Greatest) and wa la hawla wa la quwwata illa billah (and there is no power and no strength except with Allah).'"
"3461","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I saw what you did (that is, gathering at night for prayer), and nothing prevented me from coming out to you except that I feared it might be made obligatory upon you."
"3462","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Last night I saw (in a dream) that two men came to me. They took me by the hand and took me out to the Sacred Land. There was a man sitting, and a man standing over his head with an iron hook in his hand. He would put it into his cheek and tear it until he brought it out at the back of his neck, then he would take it out and put it into his other cheek, and this (first) cheek would heal. He kept doing this to him. I asked: 'What is this?' They both said: 'Go on.' So I went on with them, and there was a man lying on his back and a man standing over his head with a large stone or a rock in his hand. He would crush the (lying man's) head with it, and the stone would roll away; when he went to fetch it, his head would return to as it was before, and he would do the same again. I asked: 'What is this?' They both said: 'Go on.' So I went on with them, and there was a house built like an oven, narrow at the top and wide at the bottom, with a fire being lit beneath it. In it were naked men and women. When the fire blazed up, they rose until they were almost coming out, and when it died down, they went back into it. I asked: 'What is this?' They both said: 'Go on.' So I went on, and there was a river of blood with a man in it, and on the bank of the river stood a man with stones in front of him. The man in the river would come forward, and when he came close to getting out, (the man on the bank) would throw a stone into his mouth and he would go back to his place. He kept doing this to him. I asked: 'What is this?' They both said: 'Go on.' So I went on, and there was a green garden, and in it a huge tree. At its root was an old man with some children around him, and near him was a man with a fire in front of him, which he was fanning and kindling. Then the two of them took me up the tree and brought me into a house; I have never seen a better house than it. In it were old men, young men, women and children. Then they took me out of it, went up the tree with me and brought me into another house that was even better and more excellent than it; in it were old men and young men. I said to them both: 'You have taken me around a great deal tonight; now tell me the reality of what I have seen.' They said: 'Very well. As for the first man you saw, he is a liar who tells a lie and that lie spreads throughout the world. What you saw will be done to him until the Day of Resurrection, then Allah Almighty will do with him whatever He wills. As for the man you saw lying on his back, he is a man to whom Allah gave the Qur'an, but he slept away from it at night and did not act upon it by day. What you saw will be done to him until the Day of Resurrection. Those you saw in the oven are the adulterers (men and women). The one you saw in the river is the one who consumed usury (riba). The old man you saw at the root of the tree is Ibrahim (peace be upon him). The children you saw are the offspring of the people. The man you saw kindling the fire is the keeper of Hell, and that (which you saw) was Hell itself. The house you entered first is the house of the believers in general, and the other house is the house of the martyrs. I am Jibril and this is Mika'il.' Then they both said to me: 'Raise your head.' I raised it, and (above) there was something like a cloud. They said: 'That is your house.' I said to them: 'Let me enter my house.' They said: 'There still remains for you a lifespan that you have not completed; had you completed it, you would have entered your house.'"
"3463","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I saw the angels washing Hamzah bin Abd al-Muttalib and Hanzalah bin al-Rahib."
"3464","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I saw Jibril; he has six hundred wings."
"3465","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I saw Ja'far bin Abi Talib as an angel, flying in Paradise with the angels with two wings."
"3466","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I saw my Lord, the Mighty and Majestic."
"3467","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I saw a young man and a young woman (together), and I feared for them both from Satan (and his whisperings)."
"3468","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I saw the devils of mankind and jinn fleeing from Umar."
"3469","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I saw Amr bin Amir al-Khuza'i dragging his intestines in the Fire, and he was the first to start (the custom of) setting loose the sa'ibah and slitting the ears of the bahirah."
"3470","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I saw Amr bin Luhayy bin Qam'ah bin Khindif, the brother of Banu Ka'b, dragging his intestines in the Fire."
"3471","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I saw Isa, Musa and Ibrahim (peace be upon them). Isa was of reddish complexion, with curly hair and a broad chest. Musa was of brown complexion, heavily built, with straight hair, as though he were one of the men of the Zutt. As for Ibrahim, look at your companion (that is, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) himself)."
"3472","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I saw in a dream that I was emigrating from Makkah to a land with date palms. My thought went to its being al-Yamamah or Hajar, but it turned out to be al-Madinah, Yathrib. And I saw in this same dream that I brandished a sword and its front part broke; that (pointed) to the losses suffered by the believers on the day of Uhud. Then I brandished it again and it became better than it had been; that (pointed) to the victory and the gathering of the believers that Allah granted. And I saw cows in it, and Allah is good. Those (cows) were the group of believers (who were martyred) on the day of Uhud, and the good was what Allah granted afterwards, that is, the reward of truthfulness that Allah granted us after the day of Badr."
"3473","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I saw some people riding upon the surface of this sea, like kings upon thrones."
"3474","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I saw in a dream as though a black woman with dishevelled hair came out of Madinah until she settled at Mahya'ah (a place). I interpreted it to mean that the epidemic of Madinah had been transferred to it (Mahya'ah)."
"3475","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I saw last night as though I were in the house of Uqbah bin Rafi', and I was brought some dates of the Ibn Tab variety. I interpreted it to mean that we will have elevation in this world and a good end in the Hereafter, and that our religion has become pure."
"3476","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I saw as though I were in a strong coat of mail, and I saw cows being slaughtered. I interpreted the strong coat of mail as Madinah and the cows as a group (of martyrs), and Allah is good."
"3477","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the night I was taken on the Night Journey (Mi'raj), I saw Musa (peace be upon him). He was of brown complexion, tall, with curly hair, as though he were one of the men of the tribe of Shanu'ah. And I saw Isa (peace be upon him); he was of medium height, of a reddish-white complexion, with straight hair. And I also saw Malik, the keeper of Hell, and the Dajjal."
"3478","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I saw that I entered Paradise, and there I found al-Rumaysa (Umm Sulaym), the wife of Abu Talhah. I heard the sound of footsteps ahead of me and asked: 'Who is this, O Jibril?' He said: 'This is Bilal.' And I saw a white palace with a girl in its courtyard. I asked: 'Whose palace is this?' It was said: 'It belongs to Umar bin al-Khattab.' I wished to enter it and look at it, but I remembered your jealousy (O Umar)."
"3479","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Guarding the frontier (ribat) for one month is better than fasting for a lifetime. Whoever dies while guarding the frontier in the path of Allah is kept safe from the greatest terror (the horror of the Day of Resurrection); his provision and the fragrance of Paradise are brought to him morning and evening, and the reward of the frontier guard (murabit) continues to be recorded for him until Allah resurrects him."
"3480","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Guarding the frontier for one day is better than fasting for a month and standing (in night prayer) during it."
"3481","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Guarding the frontier for one day in the path of Allah is more excellent than fasting for a month and standing (in night prayer) during it. Whoever dies while doing so is protected from the trial of the grave, and his deeds continue to grow until the Day of Resurrection."
"3482","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Guarding the frontier for one day in the path of Allah is better than the world and everything on it. A space in Paradise the size of the whip of one of you is better than the world and everything on it. And a single going out by the servant in the path of Allah, in the evening or in the morning, is better than the world and everything on it."
"3483","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Guarding the frontier for a day and a night is better than fasting for a month and standing (in night prayer) during it. If he dies while guarding the frontier, the deeds he used to do continue (to be credited) for him, his provision also continues, and he is kept safe from the one who puts to trial."
"3484","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It may be that a dishevelled person, who is pushed away from doors, were he to swear an oath by Allah, Allah would fulfil it."
"3485","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O my Lord, help me and do not help (anyone) against me; grant me victory and do not grant (anyone) victory over me; plan for me and do not let (anyone's) plan be against me; guide me and make guidance easy for me; and help me against whoever transgresses against me. O Allah, make me grateful to You, remembering You, fearing You, obedient to You, humble before You, sighing (in devotion) and turning to You. O my Lord, accept my repentance, wash away my sin, answer my supplication, make my proof firm, guide my heart, make my tongue upright and remove the rancour from my heart."
"3486","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O my Lord, forgive me and accept my repentance; indeed You alone are the Oft-Accepting of repentance, the Most Forgiving."
"3487","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It may be that a person with two worn-out garments, who is paid no attention, were he to swear an oath by Allah, Allah would fulfil it."
"3488","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It may be that a fasting person gains nothing from his fast except hunger, and it may be that one who stands (in prayer) at night gains nothing from his standing except wakefulness."
"3489","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""How many a low-hanging cluster of dates is (ready) in Paradise for Ibn al-Dahdahah!"
"3490","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It may be that the share of one who stands (in prayer) from his standing is only wakefulness, and it may be that the share of a fasting person from his fast is only hunger and thirst."
"3491","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah have mercy on my brother Yusuf. Had the messenger come to me after such a long imprisonment, I would have responded at once, when he said: 'Go back to your king and ask him: what was the matter with the women (who cut their hands)?'"
"3492","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah have mercy on a person who spoke and gained benefit, or remained silent and stayed safe."
"3493","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah have mercy on a person who prays four rak'ahs before Asr."
"3494","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah have mercy on a man who gets up at night and prays, and wakes his wife so that she prays too; and if she refuses, he sprinkles water on her face. And may Allah have mercy on a woman who gets up at night and prays, and wakes her husband so that he prays too; and if he refuses, she sprinkles water on his face."
"3495","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah have mercy on a servant who is lenient when he sells, lenient when he buys, lenient when he repays a debt, and lenient also when he demands repayment of a debt."
"3496","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah have mercy on a servant who spoke good and so gained benefit, or kept silent from evil and so remained safe."
"3497","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah have mercy on a servant who spoke and so gained benefit, or kept silent and so remained safe."
"3498","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah have mercy on so-and-so; he has reminded me of such-and-such verses which I had left out from such-and-such a surah."
"3499","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah have mercy on Lut (peace be upon him); he used to take refuge in a strong support. And whatever prophet Allah sent after him, He sent him only with a strong clan (support) among his people."
"3500","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah have mercy on Musa (peace be upon him); he was hurt with more than this, and he was patient."
"3501","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May the mercy of Allah be upon us and upon Musa (peace be upon him). Had he been patient, he would have seen wondrous things from his companion (Khidr, peace be upon him)."
"3502","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not turn away the one who asks (empty-handed), even if it is only with a burnt hoof."
"3503","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Return the martyrs to their (original) resting places (graves)."
"3504","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man's sending a messenger to someone (to announce his coming) is itself his asking for permission."
"3505","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Close up your rows, bring them near to one another and keep your necks level. By the One in whose Hand is my soul! I see the devils entering through the gaps in the rows just like small lambs."
"3506","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The pleasure of the Lord lies in the pleasure of the father, and the displeasure of the Lord lies in the displeasure of the father."
"3507","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The pleasure of the Lord lies in the pleasure of the parents, and His displeasure lies in the displeasure of them both."
"3508","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Her (the virgin girl's) consent is her silence."
"3509","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am pleased for my Ummah with whatever Ibn Umm Abd (Abdullah bin Mas'ud) is pleased with for it."
"3510","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May the nose of that man be rubbed in the dust (in disgrace) in whose presence I was mentioned and he did not send blessings upon me; may the nose of that man be rubbed in the dust upon whom Ramadan came and then passed before he was forgiven; and may the nose of that man be rubbed in the dust whose parents reached old age in his presence and yet they did not cause him to enter Paradise."
"3511","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May he be disgraced, may he be disgraced, may he be disgraced: the one whose parents, or one of them, reach old age in his presence, and yet he does not (by serving them) enter Paradise."
"3512","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Pen has been lifted from three: from the insane person who is deprived of his reason until he recovers, from the sleeper until he wakes up, and from the child until he reaches puberty."
"3513","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Pen has been lifted from three: from the sleeper until he wakes up, from the afflicted person until he recovers, and from the child until he grows up."
"3514","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Pen has been lifted from three: from the sleeper until he wakes up, from the child until he grows into youth, and from the insane person until he comes to his senses."
"3515","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""(The sin of) mistakes, forgetfulness and whatever they are compelled to do has been pardoned for my Ummah."
"3516","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I was taken up to Sidrat al-Muntaha (the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary), whose furthest reach is in the seventh heaven. Its fruits were like the (large) jars of Hajar and its leaves were like the ears of elephants. There were four rivers there, two outward and two hidden. The two outward rivers were the Nile and the Euphrates, and the two hidden ones were two rivers of Paradise. And three vessels were brought to me: one containing milk, one containing honey and one containing wine. I took the vessel with milk and drank, and it was said to me: 'You have attained the fitrah (natural disposition), you and your Ummah.'"
"3517","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The two (Sunnah) rak'ahs of Fajr are better than the world and everything in it."
"3518","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Two light rak'ahs, which you regard as insignificant and merely voluntary, that this person adds to his deeds, are more beloved to him than the rest of your world."
"3519","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ramadan is a blessed month. In it the gates of Paradise are opened, the gates of Hell are closed and the devils are chained, and every night a caller calls out: 'O seeker of good, come forward! And O seeker of evil, desist!'"
"3520","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Children of Isma'il! Learn archery, for your father (Isma'il, peace be upon him) was an archer."
"3521","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Going to the Friday prayer is obligatory upon every adult."
"3522","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Those who show mercy, the Most Merciful, the Blessed and Exalted, shows mercy to them. Show mercy to those on the earth, and the One above the heaven will show mercy to you."
"3523","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The rider should stay behind the funeral procession, the one walking may walk wherever he wishes around it, and the funeral prayer is to be offered for a child."
"3524","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A lone rider is a devil, two riders are (also) two devils, and three riders are a caravan."
"3525","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The rider should travel behind the funeral procession, and the one walking may walk behind it, in front of it, and on its right and its left, close to it. The funeral prayer should be offered for a miscarried child, and supplication should be made for his parents for forgiveness and mercy."
"3526","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The good dream of a righteous man is one of forty-six parts of prophethood."
"3527","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A good dream is glad tidings which the believer sees himself, or which is seen for him."
"3528","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A righteous dream is one of twenty-five parts of prophethood."
"3529","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A righteous dream is one of seventy parts of prophethood."
"3530","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A righteous dream is one of forty-six parts of prophethood."
"3531","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A righteous dream is from Allah and a bad dream is from Satan. So when one of you sees something he dislikes, let him (lightly) spit dryly to his left three times as soon as he wakes up, and seek refuge with Allah from its evil; then it will not harm him."
"3532","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A righteous dream is from Allah and a bad dream is from Satan. So whoever sees a dream and dislikes something in it, let him spit dryly to his left and seek refuge with Allah from Satan; then it will not harm him. And let him not tell anyone about it. And if he sees a good dream, let him rejoice, and let him not tell it to anyone except someone he loves."
"3533","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Dreams are of three kinds: glad tidings from Allah, the thoughts of the self, and frightening from Satan. So when one of you sees a dream that pleases him, he may relate it to someone if he wishes; and if he sees something he dislikes, let him not relate it to anyone, and let him get up and pray. And I dislike (seeing in a dream) a collar around the neck, and I like a shackle on the feet; the shackle on the feet is a sign of steadfastness in the religion."
"3534","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Dreams are of three kinds: some of them are frightening fancies from Satan to grieve the son of Adam; some are what a man is concerned with while awake, so he sees it in his sleep; and some are one of forty-six parts of prophethood."
"3535","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A dream remains like a bird (suspended in the air) as long as it is not interpreted; then when it is interpreted, it comes to pass. So do not relate it except to a sincere friend or a person of sound opinion."
"3536","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""(A good) dream is from Allah and (a bad) dream is from Satan. So when one of you sees something he dislikes, let him spit dryly to his left three times, seek refuge with Allah from Satan the accursed three times, and turn over from the side he was lying on."
"3537","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Usury (riba) has seventy-two doors. The least of them is equal to a man committing incest with his own mother, and the greatest usury is a man's tongue-lashing against the honour of his brother."
"3538","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Usury (riba) has seventy-three doors."
"3539","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Usury (riba) has seventy-three doors. The least of them is equal to a man committing incest with his own mother, and the greatest usury is (attacking) the honour of a Muslim man."
"3540","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Usury (riba) has seventy doors, and shirk is likewise (having seventy degrees)."
"3541","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Usury (riba) is equal to seventy sins, the least of which is equal to a man committing incest with his own mother."
"3542","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Usury (riba), however much it increases, its end result is only towards decrease."
"3543","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man has more right to the front part of his mount, and if he (gets up for a short while and) returns, he has more right to his place as well."
"3544","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man has more right to his place; and if he goes out for some need of his and then returns, he still has more right to his place."
"3545","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man is upon the religion (way and manner) of his close friend, so let each of you look at whom he takes as a close friend."
"3546","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The stoning is an expiation for the (sin) that she committed."
"3547","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The womb (kinship) is a branch hanging from the Throne."
"3548","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The womb (kinship) is a branch derived from the name of the Most Merciful (al-Rahman). Allah says: Whoever joins you, I will join him, and whoever cuts you off, I will cut him off."
"3549","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The womb (kinship) is hanging from the Throne, and it says: Whoever joins me, may Allah join him, and whoever cuts me off, may Allah cut him off."
"3550","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""With Allah, mercy has one hundred parts. He distributed one part among the creation and kept ninety-nine parts with Himself for the Day of Resurrection."
"3551","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Provision seeks out the servant more intensely than even his death does."
"3552","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Breastfeeding makes unlawful the same relations that birth (blood kinship) makes unlawful."
"3553","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Thunder is an angel from among the angels of Allah, appointed over the clouds. He has whips of fire with which he drives the clouds wherever Allah wills."
"3554","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ruqba (saying: if you die before me this thing is mine, and if I die first it is yours) is permissible."
"3555","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The raqub (bereft one) is the woman none of whose children dies (during her lifetime)."
"3556","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The raqub (bereft one) is the one who has no forerunner (a child who has gone ahead to Paradise)."
"3557","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The true raqub (bereft one) is the one who has children, then he dies without having sent any of them ahead (during his lifetime)."
"3558","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A caravan that has bells with it, the angels do not accompany it."
"3559","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Black Stone and the Station of Ibrahim are two rubies from among the rubies of Paradise."
"3560","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Going out in the way of Allah for one evening or one morning is better than the world and everything in it."
"3561","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A pledged animal may be ridden, and it may also be milked."
"3562","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A pledged animal may be ridden in return for its upkeep, and when a milch animal is pledged, its milk may also be drunk in return for its upkeep."
"3563","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The wind is sent as a punishment for some people and as a mercy for others."
"3564","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The wind is from the mercy of Allah; it brings mercy and it brings punishment. So when you see it, do not revile it; rather, ask Allah for its good and seek refuge with Allah from its evil."
